{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaSqGXcXV2HXMfBfDMsh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I proved `length_myRev` in `Main.lean`, and `lean Main.lean` now runs with no errors or warnings.\n\n```lean\ntheorem length_myRev (xs : List α) : (myRev xs).length = xs.length := by\n  induction xs with\n  | nil => rfl\n  | cons x xs ih => simp [myRev, ih]\n```\n\nThe proof works by induction on the list:\n- **Empty list:** `myRev []` is `[]` by definition, so both lengths are 0 and `rfl` closes it.\n- **Non-empty list (`x :: xs`):** `simp` expands `myRev` to `myRev xs ++ [x]`. It then uses the standard rule that the length of `a ++ b` is the length of `a` plus the length of `b`. The induction hypothesis turns the goal into `xs.length + 1 = xs.length + 1`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":435,"cache_read_input_tokens":7851,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":435},"output_tokens":287,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"138afa87-79dc-425d-9d65-2779f43dcc07","uuid":"c11f97ad-e50f-4189-92b3-2b6f742e7940","timestamp":"2026-10-31T14:08:17.071Z","request_id":"req_011CgaSqGHUtZkzb6KQUcuCr"}
